Am I the only one still using (the excellent, free and somewhat still 
updated) Gravity? I am still thankful to the kind soul who recommended 
it to me when my newsreading stumbled from "pine" (on Unix) to the 
Windows platform.

MicroPlanet Gravity (the original Gravity, "abandonware"-ish): 
http://lightning.prohosting.com/~tbates/gravity/

Super Gravity (slightly updated by the original programmer): 
http://lightning.prohosting.com/~tbates/gravity/super.html

Gravity Open Source (OS rewrite, my choice, latest updated): 
http://lightning.prohosting.com/~tbates/gravity/status.html

If someone has something even better to recommend, I'd be happy to hear 
about it though. Perhaps there is some good reason that I seldom hear 
anyone else speaking up for it these days.

